callMethod [SimTalk]
Calls a method of the PythonModule designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.callMethod(VariableName:string, MethodName:string[, 
Argument:any, ...]) -> any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter VariableName of data type string designates the name of the Python variable.
• The parameter MethodName of data type string designates the name of the SimTalk method.
• The optional parameters Argument of data type any designate additional arguments that you can
specify.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
Example
Suppose your Python code in the PythonModule looks like this.
class ValuePair:
def __init__(self, Val1, Val2):
    self.Val1 = Val1
    self.Val2 = Val2
def getSumString(self, prefix, suffix):
    return prefix + str(self.Val1 + self.Val2) + suffix
vp = ValuePair(12, 23)
Our SimTalk code, which we call in a Method, looks like this:
print PyClassMethod.callMethod("vp", "getSumString", "Sum=", "m") 
-- returns the string "Sum=35m" in the Console
callMethod [SimTalk]
11-3750 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

