callMethodKw [SimTalk]
Calls a method of the PythonModule designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.callMethodKw(VariableName:string, MethodName:string[, 
Positionargument:any, ...] [, Keywordargument:any[] ]) -> any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter VariableName of data type string designates the name of the Python variable.
• The parameter MethodName of data type string designates the name of the SimTalk method.
• The optional parameters Positionargument of data type any designate additional position arguments
that you can specify.
• The optional parameters Keywordargument of data type any designate additional keyword arguments
that you can specify.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
Example
Suppose your Python code in the PythonModule looks like this.
class ValuePair:
def __init__(self, Val1, Val2):
    self.Val1 = Val1
    self.Val2 = Val2
def getSumString(self, prefix, suffix):
    return prefix + str(self.Val1 + self.Val2) + suffix
vp = ValuePair(12, 23)
callMethodKw [SimTalk]
11-3752 Plant Simulation Help
