importPythonModule [SimTalk]
Accesses methods and attributes of another Plant Simulation PythonModule in the PythonModule
designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<PlantSimulation-Path>.importPythonModule(Plant Simulation PythonModule) -> 
Python module object
Parameter
The parameter Plant Simulation PythonModule designates the name of the Plant Simulation
PythonModule.
Return Value
The return value is the Python module object.
Example
// Let's assume that we have a PythonModule object in the same frame as the 
current running PythonModule
// with the name 'MathModule' and this module has the function multiply 
defined.
import PlantSimulation as ps
// This imports the module and assigns it to the variable 'mm'
mm = ps.importPythonModule(current.MathModule)
// Now we can call the function 'multiply' like this:
print(mm.multiply(3,4))
importPythonModule [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3757
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

set [SimTalk]
Sets the value of the Python variable of the PythonModule designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.set(VariableName:string, Value:any)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter VariableName of data type string designates the name of the Python variable.
• The parameter Value of data type any designates the value of the Python variable.
Example
PythonModule.set("BatchSize", 40)
See also
get [SimTalk]
Read-Only Attributes of the PythonModule
Read-Only Attributes of the PythonModule
The PythonModule provides the _Read-Only Attributes of All Objects.
You can query the values of the read-only attributes, but you cannot set them as Plant Simulation
computes the value for the point-in-time at which you query it. In most cases a read-only attribute
corresponds to an unavailable dialog item on one of the tabs of the object, for example on the tab
Statistics.
To view all of the methods, read-only attributes, and attributes of the object, open the window Show
Attributes and Methods. The figure below illustrates the information using the example of the object
Station.
set [SimTalk]
11-3758 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Select Show Attributes and Methods on the context menu of the Class Library to show the methods,
read-only attributes, and attributes of the selected Class [general description].
• Press the F8 key or click Show Attributes and Methods on the Home ribbon tab of the Frame into
which you inserted an instance to show the methods, read-only attributes, and attributes of the
selected Instance [general description].
To query the value of a read-only attribute, you might, for example, type:
print MyPythonModule.UUID
